    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116157" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠλεσί-καρπος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>losing its fruit,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰτέαι ὠ.,</span> because they shed their
			fruits before ripening, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.510
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.1.3
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρινεός</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.9.14
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠ. τύμπανον</span> the
			kettledrum in the mysteries of Cybele, <i>because the priests who
				beat it were eunuchs,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.283
			</span></i>: dub. sens. in <i><span class="en">
				Cerc.
				6.14
			</span></i>.</div>
